            <ArticleTitle>The &quot;learned pain syndrome&quot;: decoding a patient's pain signals.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-6, 59-61, 64</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Learned pain is a distinct entity with its own set of symptoms, diagnostic criteria, and treatment methods. Recognition of the condition by health professionals is necessary for proper patient management and will facilitate further research and appropriate training.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
